course: dictionary
lesson: 9317
title: What is a speller?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A speller is a person who spells words. Context helps you work out the meaning: «She's a good speller» tells you a speller is someone who spells words well or badly, so spelling is a skill you can be good or poor at.
explain: Reading and spelling are different skills. «Even keen readers can be weak spellers, because reading skims words without studying every letter.» So a good reader is not always a good speller, and you need to look closely at letters to spell well.
explain: Spelling does not measure how clever you are. Many smart people find spelling hard, including some with dyslexia. «The best news for spellers: a prefix never changes the spelling of the root word.» That is a useful clue to check before you guess at a spelling.
fact: A speller is a person who spells words, and you can be a good speller or a poor one.
fact: In the US and Canada, a speller can also be a school book of spelling lists and exercises.
fact: A spell-checker on a computer is sometimes called a speller.
fact: In a spelling bee, the contestants are called spellers.
fact: Being a poor speller has nothing to do with being clever.
exercise: «She is a good speller.» What is a speller? | A type of pencil | A long word for a dictionary | A kind of fish | *A person who spells words
exercise: In a spelling bee, the people taking part are called what? | *Spellers | Judges | Readers | Teachers
exercise: In US schools, what is a speller? | *A school book of spelling lists and exercises | A map of the school | A ruler | A diary
test: «Even keen readers can be weak spellers.» What does this tell us? | *Being a keen reader does not mean you spell well | Keen readers never make mistakes | Spelling is only for adults | Good readers are always good spellers
test: A spell-checker on a computer is sometimes called what? | A keyboard | A printer | A reader | *A speller
exam: According to «The best news for spellers», what never changes when a prefix is added? | The sound of the word | The number of letters | *The spelling of the root word | The meaning of the root word
